{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/962395-monsters-from-other-rpgs-unremitting-horror-flame-princess-etc-in-cofd","id":962395,"title":"Monsters from other RPGs (Unremitting Horror, Flame Princess, etc) in CofD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-02T11:24:20-07:00","id":962395,"title":"Monsters from other RPGs (Unremitting Horror, Flame Princess, etc) in CofD?","content":"I was wondering, has anyone ever tried to adapt monsters from other tabletop settings to ChroD? I know there's plenty of Delta Green/Call of Cthulhu influence both ways, but has anyone tried it with any other monsters?<br /> <br /> What made me think of this idea was the Book of Unremitting Horror. Despite the name, it only occasionally reaches Vile Darkness-level unintentional silliness, and is for the most part a very interesting urban-fantasy-personal-horror bestiary of completely original monsters. The illustrations are fantastically gross, too. It also comes with a couple nice adventures that could easily be adapted into Blue Book or Hunter stories, and the creatures themselves could be adapted into ChroD in any number of ways. <br /> <br /> For example, one of them is a sort of unborn god of murder that a cult of serial killers is trying to breed (yes, it does get pretty over the top), and it would be very easy to use that as a Hunter antagonist. <br /> <br /> Lusus Naturae and the Teratic Tome are for LotFP and assume a fantasy setting, but a lot of the ideas in them (especially LN) could easily be used as springboards or inspiration for ChroD antagonists. There are a lot of really wonderful, often darkly whimsical ideas there, and a lot that would be especially good for some really freaky Changeling antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T11:52:54-07:00","id":962410,"title":"","content":"Book of Unremitting Horror is ace. Funnily enough, one of the most underwhelmimg monsters in it (The Practice, the demonic surgeons) went on to become the star of the single most horrifying published adventure I've ever read, Invasive Procedure.<br /> <br /> Whatever the self-harm mummies were, those were my favorite. Brrrrr. Maybe I'll try to convert them? Between the Horror rules and all of Hunter's Dread Powers, it can't be that hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:04:55-07:00","id":962421,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine once ran a basic mortals game that included the Torture Dogs (I think, it was a good number of years ago) from BoUH. Pretty fun game it was too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:35:01-07:00","id":962443,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/782555-gurps-monster-conversions\">Here </a>is a thread containing write-ups for various GURPS monsters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:59:14-07:00","id":962452,"title":"","content":"I sadly haven't had time to read as much Unknown Armies as I'd like, but there are plenty of wonderful things there you could bring into ChroD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-03-2016, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T16:38:38-07:00","id":962563,"title":"","content":"I had a variety of slimes and oozes as Pandorans in a game. While obviously not confined to other RPGs, they were based on various 3.5 Monster Manuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T07:59:24-07:00","id":962826,"title":"","content":"I'm getting back to the GURPS thread pretty soon, but I own BoUR as well.<br /> <br /> I especially like Strap Throat, so:<br /> <br /> <b>Strap Throat, the Geist of Mary Beth Spaulding<br /> <br /> Virtue:</b> Avenger<br /> <br /> <b>Vice</b>: Vicious<br /> <br /> <b>Anchors: </b>As an Underworld shade, Strap Throat does not have permanent anchors. however, if the ritual to summon her is performed successfully and she chooses to manifest, her &quot;mirror&quot;, and her target serve for the duration of her stay on the mortal coil. While she regularly patrols the woods where she lived, in truth this is due to an Avernian Gate that was torn open there by her death-when it opens, she pops out, wanders her grave site for a bit, then goes back in before the Gate closes.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 3<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Power 8, Finesse 3, Resistance 9<br /> <br /> <b>Corpus: </b>14<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower: </b>10 <br /> <br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <br /> <b>Speed: </b>21<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative: </b>11<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <br /> <b>Numen:</b> Blast (Destructive scream), Emotional Aura (remorse, shame), Seek, Know Soul<br /> <br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Materialize, Fetter<br /> <br /> <b>Influences</b>: Anchor 1, Retribution 3<br /> <br /> <b>Essence: </b>20<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Strap Throat cannot speak without unleashing her Blast Numen, although she understands all languages (unfortunately, Mary Beth was never taught how to read, so communicating with her involves either a lot of charades or a lot of pain). In addition, she can only Manifest out of a mirror (here meaning any reflective surface), with at least her foot still inside whatever she is reaching out of-she cannot move except along the surface mirror, but it doesn't cost her Essence to jump from mirror to mirror (she withdraws into her current host and vanished only to appear in another mirror nearby). This does not affect her Defense (damaging the mirror doesn't hurt Strap Throat, and she dodges by strategically withdrawing herself into the mirror).<br /> <br /> <b>Bane</b>: Tears of genuine remorse.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T11:06:07-07:00","id":962895,"title":"","content":"That is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T21:18:40-07:00","id":966594,"title":"","content":"Given the strong fantasy vibe in Changeling, that would probably be another good place to work in some D&amp;D/Pathfinder monsters. The Hedge is probably the only place in ChroD where you can throw a squad of orcs at your players. I've always thought the Autumn Court would love tabletop games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T21:48:58-07:00","id":966607,"title":"","content":"I haven't tried to implement it yet, but I'd like to put mind-flayers in a CofD campaign. Perhaps as some sort of Abyssal intruders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T21:53:18-07:00","id":966611,"title":"","content":"Eh, I kinda think they're a bit too normal for the Abyss. I'd make them Gentry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T04:52:53-07:00","id":966707,"title":"","content":"What's wrong with making them parasitic entities from the far future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:37:36-07:00","id":966823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/962395-monsters-from-other-rpgs-unremitting-horror-flame-princess-etc-in-cofd?p=966707#post966707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's wrong with making them parasitic entities from the far future?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not mutually exclusive.The Abyss merely seemed like the closest thing to the Far Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:31:52-07:00","id":966894,"title":"","content":"I'm just thinking that &quot;psychic brain eating octopus headed humanoids&quot; is a bit too understandable for the Abyss. I can't really get behind an Abyssal unless it's at least slightly a memetohazard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:04:02-07:00","id":968981,"title":"","content":"This would be fun with videogame monsters too. Has anyone written up anything from the Souls series or Bloodborne?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}